:Gram|g]]) peeled raw [[cookbook:shrimp|shrimp]]\n* 1 [[cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 3 cloves [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* 12 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]] (340 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) of [[cookbook:beer|beer]]\n* [[cookbook:Tabasco Sauce|Tabasco sauce]]\n* [[cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[cookbook:pepper|Pepper]]\n* [[cookbook:Butter|Butter]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Combine onion, garlic, shrimp, and beer in a plastic or glass bowl. \n# Add as much Tabasco as you'd like (start with 1 tbsp) and some salt and pepper to taste. \n# Cover and [[cookbook:marinating|marinate]] overnight. \n# Remove shrimp from marinade, and discard marinade. \n# Melt some butter in a pan and [[cookbook:sauté|sauté]] shrimp until pink and done. Don't overcook the shrimp or they'll be rubbery. You can also [[cookbook:grilling|grill]] the shrimp. \n\n[[Category:Pescatarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beer]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Marinade recipes]]\n[[Category:Sautéed recipes]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Beer Marinated Shrimp","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 pounds (900 g) peeled raw shrimp","sourceText":"2 pounds (900 g) peeled raw shrimp","amountText":"2 pounds (900 g) peeled raw shrimp","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 onion, sliced","sourceText":"1 onion, sliced","amountText":"1 onion, sliced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 cloves garlic, minced","sourceText":"3 cloves garlic, minced","amountText":"3 cloves garlic, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"12 ounces (340 ml) of beer","sourceText":"12 